        "harness": "native",
        "goal": "Fix the LRU cache in src/lru.js so that reading a key refreshes its recency (upstream prompt: set a,b; get a; set c must evict b, and get a still returns 1) and the frozen upstream suite passes.",
        "prompt": "# Bug report: LruCache evicts a key that was just read\n\nWe use `LruCache` to cache rendered templates. With a capacity of 2, running\n`set('a', 1)`, `set('b', 2)`, `get('a')`, `set('c', 3)` evicts `a` even though it was\nthe most recently used entry, so `get('a')` afterwards returns `undefined`. The expected\nbehavior is that `b` gets evicted and `get('a')` still returns `1`.\n\nThe test suite in this workspace reproduces the problem. Find the bug in the source and\nfix it so the whole suite passes.\n\n---\nExecution workspace (this is an isolated checkout of the upstream benchmark):\n- Fix only `tasks/02-lru-cache/workspace/src/`.\n- The frozen test is `tasks/02-lru-cache/workspace/lru.test.js`; run it with:\n  node --test --test-reporter=tap tasks/02-lru-cache/workspace/lru.test.js\n- Do not edit the test file or `package.json`, and do not weaken the tests.\n- Report what you changed and the test result.\n",
