        "id": "upstream-latitude-14-event-bus",
        "revision": "fixture@3b58b9e18466d622",
        "repo": ".ops/benchmark-repos/latitude-dev--coding-agent-benchmark",
        "baseCommit": "cd28f3965d4d9d2fc9a49faca573f16b5102b488",
        "harness": "native",
        "goal": "Fix once()/replay behaviour in src/once.js so a once handler runs exactly once even when a handler re-emits the event, and the frozen upstream suite passes.",
        "prompt": "# Bug report: a once() handler ran twice during a re-entrant emit\n\nWe use the bus to coordinate state sync. A high-priority handler on `sync` re-broadcasts\nthe event exactly one time when it first sees it (it emits `sync` again from inside its\nown handler). A listener registered with `once(bus, 'sync', handler)` was invoked twice:\nfirst with the re-broadcast payload, then again with the original one. Expected `once`\nto invoke its handler exactly one time no matter how the emits nest. Plain back-to-back\nemits behave correctly, so this only shows up when an emit happens inside a handler.\n\nThe test suite in this workspace reproduces the problem. Find the bug in the source and\nfix it so the whole suite passes.\n\n---\nExecution workspace (this is an isolated checkout of the upstream benchmark):\n- Fix only `tasks/14-event-bus/workspace/src/`.\n- The frozen test is `tasks/14-event-bus/workspace/event-bus.test.js`; run it with:\n  node --test --test-reporter=tap tasks/14-event-bus/workspace/event-bus.test.js\n- Do not edit the test file or `package.json`, and do not weaken the tests.\n- Report what you changed and the test result.\n",
